/-!
# Original-root reductions for 14.7.73

The marking is inherited from the original H→S₅ map and its natural-module
marking. The two-core remains O₂(K)=K∩O₂(H). The algebra constructs Sylow
preimages, lifts root generation, identifies the normal ordered root product
with O₂(K), and proves U≤E and centrality of E/U before recognition.

The applications feed these results into the elementary-quotient,
commutator-generation and canonical-cover leaves. Completing 14.7.73 still
requires the original marked projective geometry and multiplicity-one
argument, E=C_P(U), the parabolic two-core/index identifications, and the
coprime fixed-kernel count. Their extra inputs are not source hypotheses.

Final 14.7.73 assembly remains here; 14.7.71–74 and the Ru assembly remain
with the parent SourceEndgame owner. Existing umbrella imports are preserved.
Source: Aschbacher–Smith, printed pp.1076–1077, manuscript of 1 March 2004.
-/
